<title>USA: Court allows Wabash buy of Fruehauf assets.</title>
<headline>Court allows Wabash buy of Fruehauf assets.</headline>
<dateline>LAFAYETTE, Ind. 1997-03-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Wabash National Corp said Friday its bid to purchase certain assets of Fruehauf Trailer Corp has been approved by the U.S. Bankruptcy Court in Wilmington, Del.</p>
<p>The purchase is valued at about $52 million.</p>
<p>The assets purchased include the Fruehauf name, all patents and trademarks, retail outlets in 31 major metropolitan markets, the aftermarket parts distribution business based in Grove City, Ohio, a specialty trailer manufacturing plant in Huntsville, Tenn., and a trailer manufacturing plant in Ft. Madison, Iowa.  </p>
<p>The purchase is subject to certain regulatory approvals.</p>
<p>Industry analysts have said that the purchase will allow Wabash, the largest U.S. manufacturer of truck trailers, to gain access to previously underserved markets.</p>
<p>			((Chicago newsdesk 312 408 8787))</p>
